@using Yello.Client.Spaces

@inject IStringLocalizer<ClientCopy> Localizer

@*
    THE ROLE CHIP. AC5; UX-DR28; DESIGN.md:169-174, :455; test-design X-8.

    DISPLAY-ONLY, AND NEVER A CONTROL. A <span> with no handler, no link, no button and no tab stop.
    A Role is changed by an Owner or Admin on the Members surface (epic 4), never from here, and a
    chip that looked operable would be a promise the product does not keep.
    SpaceSwitcherGateTests.The_Role_chip_is_never_interactive holds the markup to that.

    BORDERED. The --role-chip fill sits at 1.05 against the bar without its hairline (X-8), so the
    border is what makes it a chip rather than a tint.

    THE ROLE VERBATIM, IN SENTENCE CASE. "Owner", "Admin", "Member", "Viewer" from the resources;
    the uppercase is .type-role-label's text-transform, which base.css withholds in Turkish, Azeri
    and Greek - so a screen reader hears the word, not its letters.
*@

<span class="role-chip type-role-label">@Localizer[RoleCopy.NameKey(Role)]</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The Role's stable code, as the server answered it for this Space on this load.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public string Role { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
